// Failure golden: a non-exhaustive match (ADR-80; ADR-54 §4.2).
// (Pathological tree: testing artifact, not pedagogy -- ADR-52 Decision C.)
//
// `Maybe(a)` has two constructors; a `case` that answers only `Some` omits
// `None`. The 1-cell MVP does no static exhaustiveness check (Maranget stays
// with the patterns bead), so the missing constructor arm degenerates to a hole
// -- and when the scrutinee IS that missing constructor (`None`), the hole is
// reached at runtime and reported as a DEFINED halt (`Blame::Hole`), not a
// panic. That runtime blame is the coverage gap made observable.
data Maybe(a) { None, Some(x: a) }

def unwrap() -> F Integer {
  case (None : Maybe(Integer)) {
    Some(x) => ret x
  }
}

unwrap()

//@ expect-blame: hole
